      "question": "Does anything need a human decision, and why?",
      "answer": "No decision needed yet. Routine oven fault, approval given, no spend cap or quote yet. Escalate only if the provider cannot confirm a visit or records of the tenant's identity stay in conflict after the reply."
    }
  ],
  "actions_claimed": [
    {
      "ledger_id": "A1",
      "description": "Recorded landlord decision 'approved' with quote 'Yes go ahead' (event 009)."
    },
    {
      "ledger_id": "A2",
      "description": "Emailed Keystone Compliance to confirm attending company, date/slot and tenant contact."
    },
    {
      "ledger_id": "A3",
      "description": "Emailed tenant that the visit is not yet confirmed and asked for best contact number."
    },
    {
      "ledger_id": "A4",
      "description": "Put job on hold (Waiting for Provider) with review 2025-08-28."
    }
  ],
  "failed_actions": [],
  "conflicts": [
    "Visit date: system 30/08/2025 10:00 (event 017, 018, 019) vs provider 'Monday morning between 10 and 12' (event 016). 30/08/2025 is a Saturday; trusted neither until provider confirms.",
    "Provider: assigned Keystone Compliance (events 012-014, 018) vs caller Isaac Palmer from Riverside Works (event 016).",
    "Tenant name: Clara (event 001, 018) vs Ruben Oakley (events 013, 014, 019) vs Grace Mercer (event 016).",
    "Tenant phone: 07700 900721 (event 014) vs 07700 900077 (event 018, 019)."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "The landlord's 'Yes go ahead' covers the provider's visit and diagnosis, not a repair spend, as no cap was given.",
    "Email on the existing thread is the right channel for both parties, as both wrote on it."
  ]
}

